body.raw:
{
  "prompt": "You are an expert technical interview coach. Read this job description and decide which interview round the candidate should prepare for.

Return ONLY a raw JSON object, no markdown fences, no commentary, with exactly these keys:
{"round_type": one of "Technical/DSA" or "System Design" or "Mixed", "level": one of "Entry" or "Mid" or "Senior", judged from the experience and responsibilities asked for, "reasoning": one or two sentences explaining the call, "topics": an array of 4 to 7 specific technical topics to focus on}

JOB DESCRIPTION:
Senior Unity engineer building mobile games in C#. Profile and optimize performance, memory usage and garbage collection across iOS and Android. Design scalable core game systems, own features end to end, and review code. 6+ years of game development, strong C# and Unity3D, mobile optimization experience.",
  "maxOutputTokens": 1024
}

{
  "prompt": "You are an expert technical interviewer writing questions for a {{round_type}} interview round.

Focus topics: {{topics}}
This is batch 1 of 4. Difficulty for this batch: {{first_rung}}.
{{level_guidance}}
Write 5 questions. Do not repeat questions from earlier batches.

Exactly ONE question in this batch must have "type": "speech". The rest are "mcq".

Never write options such as "All of the above", "None of the above" or "Both A and B", and never refer to an option by its letter or position anywhere, including in the explanation. The options will be shown in a different order.

Return ONLY a raw JSON array, no markdown fences, no commentary. Each element:
{"question": the question text, "type": "mcq" or "speech", "options": array of exactly 4 short answer strings (empty array when type is speech), "correct_index": 0-based index of the right option (use -1 when type is speech), "explanation": for mcq why the right answer is right, for speech the key points a strong spoken answer must cover, "category": a short topic label such as "Arrays" or "Caching"}",
  "maxOutputTokens": 4096
}

{
  "prompt": "You are grading a candidate's spoken answer in a technical interview. Be fair but rigorous, and judge it against what is expected at {{level}} level.

QUESTION: {{speech_question}}

KEY POINTS A STRONG ANSWER COVERS: {{speech_key_points}}

CANDIDATE TRANSCRIPT: {{candidate_transcript}}

The transcript came from speech to text, so ignore grammar, filler words, and transcription noise. Judge the substance.

Return ONLY a raw JSON object, no markdown fences, no commentary:
{"score": integer 0 to 100, "feedback": two or three sentences on what landed and what was missing}",
  "maxOutputTokens": 1024
}

{
  "prompt": "You are a technical interview coach writing a short debrief for a candidate who just finished a {{round_type}} practice session at {{level}} level.

Focus topics for the role: {{topics}}
Per question results, formatted as category/type/outcome: Memory Management/mcq/correct; Memory Management/speech/42 of 100; Unity Architecture/mcq/wrong; Mobile Performance/mcq/correct; Unity Architecture/speech/81 of 100

Do not use em dashes anywhere. Return ONLY a raw JSON object, no markdown fences, no commentary:
{"overall_readiness": two or three sentences on how ready they are for this round, "strengths": array of 2 to 3 short strings, "focus_areas": array of 2 to 3 short strings, "tip": one concrete thing to do before the next session}",
  "maxOutputTokens": 1024
}
